  "rationale": "The question asks for the initial step. Elevation is the first conservative measure before escharotomy if vascular compromise persists.",
  "optionExplanations": {
    "A": "Escarotomy is used if circumferential burn eschar causes vascular compromise, but it is not the initial step.",
    "B": "Dressings do not relieve the constrictive effect of a circumferential burn.",
    "C": "Elevation reduces oedema and is the initial step to help prevent distal ischaemia.",
    "D": "Fasciotomy is reserved for compartment syndrome, not the first measure for a circumferential burn.",
    "E": "Debridement is not the immediate step to prevent distal ischaemia."
  },
